<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Tale of Kieu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 19th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Truyện Kiều, The Tale of Kiều</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tale of Kieu, or Truyện Kiều, is an epic poem by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-du">Nguyễn Du</a>, written in the early nineteenth century in chữ Nôm script and in the six-eight lục bát verse form. Adapted from a Chinese novel, it tells of Thúy Kiều, a young woman who sells herself to save her family and endures fifteen years of suffering. It is the best-known work of Vietnamese literature and is widely quoted.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-tale-of-kieu.jpg" alt="The Tale of Kieu" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nôm Foundation · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kim_V%C3%A2n_Ki%E1%BB%81u_t%C3%A2n_truy%E1%BB%87n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
